cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "precis-mcp: a Model Context Protocol server for papers, documents, and agent state"
abstract: >-
  precis-mcp is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives
  language-model agents a small, uniform API for reading, writing, and
  searching across scientific papers, documents, personal state, code,
  and cached tool calls. Small-model-friendly (7B-class agents are the
  design target), it exposes a handful of typed verbs over a large
  catalogue of content kinds, with per-chunk hybrid lexical/semantic
  search, provenance-tracked claims, and a web interface. Content is
  stored in PostgreSQL with pgvector.
